From f2a385c4f134617f0eb67856b6e966167b6623a7 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: AshFall UI <ui@ashfall.local>
Date: Sun, 15 Nov 2026 16:28:21 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] SystemUI: AshFall PlayTime battery indicator

Stock Android predicts remaining battery life from long-term averages that
include hours of standby, so a handheld shows "18 h remaining" and then
collapses to two hours under a 3D emulator. Add an active-only estimate to
the status bar: the current is averaged over a rolling window of the
current screen-on session and turned into remaining time (discharging) or
time to full (charging).

The estimator is pure Java with an injected clock, no Android dependency,
so the maths is unit tested on the host: window expiry, the screen-off
purge, "--" before one full interval, charging time-to-full, FULL, the four
time formats, the >48h cap, the charge-counter current fallback and the tap
cycle.

Telemetry comes from BatteryManager, not from a daemon property: a coredomain
may not read sysfs_batteryinfo (platform neverallow) and on the RP5 those
nodes carry a vendor label. The sticky ACTION_BATTERY_CHANGED broadcast
supplies level, voltage, charging state and the charge counter (capacity is
derived from counter and level). BATTERY_PROPERTY_CURRENT_NOW supplies the
current in uA, rectified to mA, but the RP5 health HAL reports
batteryCurrentMicroamps = 0 even under load, so when it says nothing the
slope of BATTERY_PROPERTY_CHARGE_COUNTER (uAh) over a >=10 s window is used
instead - that counter is the only real current the platform exposes here
(dumpsys battery "Charge counter" moves). Unsupported properties stay
unknown and render "--"; nothing reads sysfs and nothing polls a service in
the background - the receivers only exist while the indicator is attached.

The status bar element is a TextView in the PhoneStatusBarView hierarchy
tinted from the same DarkIconDispatcher source as the clock, placed left or
right of the battery or the clock, or in the battery percentage slot. The
status bar root in this tree is still the View status_bar.xml, but the
battery percentage is Compose (BatteryWithPercent), so REPLACE_PERCENT also
suppresses the stock percentage there.

Settings are read from persist.ashfall.batt.*. They are written by Settings
in another process, where no change notification reaches SystemUI
(SystemProperties.addChangeCallback only reports changes made by the writing
process), so the indicator re-reads the validated schema on a 2 s
main-thread tick and only notifies on a real change. Screen state comes from
ACTION_SCREEN_ON/OFF (Dependency.get(ScreenLifecycle) is not a provider in
this tree), so sampling still pauses with the screen off and the estimator
still purges its window on wake. A missing view, a missing broadcast or an
unsupported battery property leaves the indicator hidden or on "--" instead
of crashing SystemUI; FULL and >48h are explicit.

